  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract activity in Illinois through FY2026 to date shows a noticeable pullback in obligations. Total obligations were $8.7B, spread across 374,003 awards, with an average award size of $23.2K. Obligations fell 30.0% year over year. The Department of Defense accounted for the largest share of buying activity with $4.2B in obligations, followed by the Department of Energy with $1.8B and the Department of Veterans Affairs with $1.6B. UCHICAGO ARGONNE, LLC was the single largest vendor with $1B in obligations, and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences led industry categories with $1B. FY2026 to date totals are partial and cover only the fiscal year to date. Historical context shows higher full-year totals in recent years, including $13.6B in FY22 and $13.4B in FY24, which frames the current fiscal-year-to-date position against prior full fiscal years. This profile highlights concentration in defense and energy buying, sizable research R&D obligations, and a high volume of relatively small awards by value.",
    "sections": [
