        "heading": "What changed in FY2026 to date compared with prior years?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 30.0% year over year in FY2026 to date. Total obligations were $8.7B, down from prior full-year totals such as $12.4B in FY25 and $13.4B in FY24. Award volume remained high at 374,003 awards, with an average award size of $23.2K. FY2026 to date totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date activity rather than a full-year count."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate Illinois federal contracting in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $4.2B in obligations. The Department of Energy and the Department of Veterans Affairs follow with $1.8B and $1.6B respectively. UCHICAGO ARGONNE, LLC is the largest vendor with $1B in obligations, and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the top industry with $1B in obligations."
      }
